  "generated_text": "First, we start with the given equation:\n\\[\nz + z^{-1} = \\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we square both sides of the equation:\n\\[\n(z + z^{-1})^2 = (\\sqrt{3})^2\n\\]\n\\[\nz^2 + 2 \\cdot z^{-1} + z^{-2} = 3\n\\]\n\\[\nz^2 + 2 + z^{-2} = 3\n\\]\n\nSubtract 2 from both sides:\n\\[\nz^2 + z^{-2} = 1\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find \\( z^{2010} + z^{-2010} \\). Notice that \\( z^{2010} = z^2 \\cdot z^{2008} \\) and \\( z^{-2010} = z^{-2} \\cdot z^{-2008} \\). This means:\n\\[\nz^{2010} + z^{-2010} = z^2 + z^{-2} = 1\n\\]\n\nThus, the value is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[1, '1']",
    "gold_answer": "We start by trying to express $z$ in a more convenient form.\nWe are given that $ z + z^{-1} = \\sqrt{3} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{2} = 2 \\cos{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}$\nSo we know that $z$ is $\\text{cis}{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}$ or $\\text{cis}{-\\frac{\\pi}{6}}$\n\nSay that $z = \\text{cis}{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}$. Then,\n$$z^{2010} = \\left(\\text{cis}{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\right)^{2010} = \\text{cis}{\\frac{2010\\pi}{6}} = \\text{cis}335\\pi = \\text{cis}\\pi = -1.$$Then $z^{-1} = -1^{-1} = -1$. So\n$$z^{2010} + z^{-2010} = -1 + (-1) = \\boxed{-2}.$$Similarly, if $z = \\text{cis}{-\\frac{\\pi}{6}}$. Then,\n$$z^{2010} = \\left(\\text{cis}{-\\frac{\\pi}{6}}\\right)^{2010} = \\text{cis}{-\\frac{2010\\pi}{6}} = \\text{cis}-335\\pi = \\text{cis}-\\pi = -1.$$Then $z^{-1} = -1^{-1} = -1$. So\n$$z^{2010} + z^{-2010} = -1 + (-1) = \\boxed{-2}.$$",
    "is_correct": false
  },
